#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23794494-b7b9-5ad4-ba11-ebd6f0094b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550449} {:answer/id #uuid "3a5b9969-07fa-546a-9da1-aef831577fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-264" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550504} {:answer/id #uuid "46d92d44-866f-550f-b83c-6f430b5c3fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550534} {:answer/id #uuid "4c68a53f-d7de-5bed-a987-bf6fbaa3cc30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "624" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550547} {:answer/id #uuid "de604167-4d91-5774-b979-150a3cf404e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-462" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550504} :answer-field/id #uuid "3af53959-1d8a-5698-92dc-98fa9d92ef56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "231b9e48-9ef0-506b-a5a1-fc73da681086" :question/math-academy-id "q-42916" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\,\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 1 & -4\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below ${a}_{14}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary row operations, let's make entries below ${a}_{14}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -13 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -13 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}\\begin{vmatrix}6 & -13 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}6 & -13 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 6\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-6(35-(-9)) \\\\  & =-264.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551268 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158027fe-d400-5403-b113-28a2067773a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550413} {:answer/id #uuid "337cbaa8-fc57-5b7c-903e-2bd27c9209af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550491} {:answer/id #uuid "aa13465f-e041-55e1-9140-2cd2282116de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550821} {:answer/id #uuid "b73a51f1-c568-5f92-aff8-42cc56eb157b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550871} {:answer/id #uuid "c02e61c6-21c0-5d92-95e2-e73618a38e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 9 & -1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550894}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550871} :answer-field/id #uuid "29c80b82-1274-56dd-b869-d31fed57239d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4038f08b-56e1-5740-bb03-adc638c1a6b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-91219" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{13}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{13}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-1){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+4{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -2 & -6\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -2 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5 & -6\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03920cc4-e1f8-50bf-92b8-43b1b2e14c0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550381} {:answer/id #uuid "240d25dd-ce33-51bd-b4d9-30068b1a023f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550455} {:answer/id #uuid "5f583757-004f-544b-ab61-0bdb788421ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -7 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550600} {:answer/id #uuid "75c87c6c-1364-57a5-9015-96559daffe3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550664} {:answer/id #uuid "9c4798fb-d6a8-5a46-9f8e-17d00a574faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550765}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550381} :answer-field/id #uuid "69e4982b-2aae-5d00-991d-b6494c4a55db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "45127938-c6a2-5a13-8b44-5358b2433862" :question/math-academy-id "q-42930" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{33}=-1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 & 8\\end{vmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 8\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ea1ce55-966d-5f10-abed-3819f8de0d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 13 & -9 & 10\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550554} {:answer/id #uuid "88557905-c296-5243-b252-30962e7378f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 10 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550712} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9b00b3-88c8-55d0-a71f-b06285ff52ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 13 & 6 & -11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550719} {:answer/id #uuid "b93f13a2-e5b1-5e21-8544-b4448537f761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 13 & -9 & 12\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550878} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7aab0a-5fbf-5e2a-a8eb-5cfb03bbb901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 13 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551051}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551051} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4767d77-4ea5-54fd-8af5-d2063ff21fec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "634c0345-e97a-5738-8ae3-640a8e78ce93" :question/math-academy-id "q-132023" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 9 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 6 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{41}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{41}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 9 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 6 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 13 & -9 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 13 & -9 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 13 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 13 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53538eaf-3ca1-53e7-9333-cb61969424e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550565} {:answer/id #uuid "55b5cc00-611f-5c77-a3e4-4fa552b677f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550574} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5a6ba5-deda-5536-8c5f-86d60dc12567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550593} {:answer/id #uuid "63aa3b56-bb47-5f40-b3a8-c0a8da00b436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 14\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550608} {:answer/id #uuid "6d228a6a-bde9-526c-92b6-f3b9c6d2dd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 14 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550638}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550638} :answer-field/id #uuid "7975514b-1327-5f70-a5a4-a2499ab3c36c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "adab6899-9f13-599d-9b9d-313f4a53055c" :question/math-academy-id "q-91173" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 14 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 14 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 14 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 14 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09186fb4-7a2e-503b-b7a3-7e5633093c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551684} {:answer/id #uuid "444b005a-5aa9-59f5-be5f-4b3fe4d7fdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551832} {:answer/id #uuid "95f59555-41e7-5c59-b9d8-5da7888a51ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552027} {:answer/id #uuid "d17d0449-be69-51f2-8c79-3f73a7a82292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552163} {:answer/id #uuid "f28cd004-e937-5e64-b735-51c637ba786e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552163} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8d06a2-6686-5f9c-8dfb-21558d785068" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "18af1f73-e41b-5d4c-86dd-e0a8cf91a4f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130861" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=6{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same  elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=6{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abff303-77dd-56d3-ad00-30620d984218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-9{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551691} {:answer/id #uuid "3bcd78ca-5e2a-5471-ad67-9be0b4d67f27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{2}-9{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551813} {:answer/id #uuid "546fa487-ed64-5369-98f9-475e837b6e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-9{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551867} {:answer/id #uuid "9e07c7bd-cab3-5881-bacb-c7528c9d2267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-9{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552046} {:answer/id #uuid "c63c696e-bb97-5da0-98e4-fe4b63225c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-9{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552136}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551867} :answer-field/id #uuid "b99d03d7-ecc8-545f-aa25-7f9a604e6a37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "262002ef-4fd0-5419-8127-789c5234e1d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130840" :question/problem "Let $$\n\\displaystyle E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $-9$ times the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-9{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552432 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ee4f79-2a09-5bc8-9e12-a444fc9edda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551790} {:answer/id #uuid "aef4e9a3-db19-5b39-af6a-00e6027ac2a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552087} {:answer/id #uuid "b8f52d67-4d5c-5ab0-aa85-311cad094cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552112} {:answer/id #uuid "ef274a2a-e6d8-50b7-8fd1-665ddd66f23f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552224} {:answer/id #uuid "fda3a50b-d040-56ba-9e2f-91e779b8b142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552252}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552112} :answer-field/id #uuid "cff42165-0565-50e9-9c24-d18be82e3972" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "46fec928-7e8c-5465-b67b-b3ef68641ebc" :question/math-academy-id "q-75114" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the  three given elementary row operations. \n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552440 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d6e35e-81a7-51c8-a7cc-f32f8bec0ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551711} {:answer/id #uuid "8f86283f-18b3-551e-a40d-cf34a8f4063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552016} {:answer/id #uuid "b16f32c5-9c6a-55cb-ad66-50b0738320e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552093} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ef215c-9e2e-51a9-8bc6-e53e4bf54b39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552147} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0a04ef-d28b-50c5-a529-054c7b32dde9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552152}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552016} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fc02b48-7c0b-5dca-8522-1bed2f8f771b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "59ac31ae-d95c-5ade-b172-6fbd672350bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-42811" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552443 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5340afab-e3d7-511b-b16e-2935f27dba7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551861} {:answer/id #uuid "95c5f066-cf63-5e7d-93b4-576c0ea73d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552026} {:answer/id #uuid "9baf77c2-c4d3-50ca-9377-291961a81d4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552042} {:answer/id #uuid "a08825d6-8a91-58f6-b54c-3b9c1e8c4422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552054} {:answer/id #uuid "ace0ae29-a086-5f8d-b958-58328df9646e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552079}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552079} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd63b2c-12c1-54cb-802c-3c21ad3aab91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "608d80e2-812d-50df-95f4-906e16812c70" :question/math-academy-id "q-42760" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}.$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08830d78-3dad-5449-8109-359dc60bc730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551681} {:answer/id #uuid "27d6879e-11ea-5047-b0de-3a3221a139a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=6{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551755} {:answer/id #uuid "ae976e85-aa05-5923-ae47-cc106ee58f91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552086} {:answer/id #uuid "d050a82d-7b03-5d25-baca-61d6a9c6aedc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552159} {:answer/id #uuid "e51b6b71-81f0-5560-af0e-fbae134fe705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552196}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552159} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d0a791f-68bf-567b-9398-0225c9085e8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "697a3132-99c3-5286-b927-185afe5caf9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75076" :question/problem "Let $$\n\\displaystyle E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $6$ times the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "244dda5b-5b90-5880-91d6-8964f79bd7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551747} {:answer/id #uuid "58869cfc-79d4-5f7b-b6a1-25e2a3bbe897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551877} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0a9f51-e34e-59e8-939a-0f36ea7dc858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551916} {:answer/id #uuid "875518a0-30c3-54be-b6df-66fbc1c064d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551993} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4aad5e-10a6-5e44-a3de-51d162a2df8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552012}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551747} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a3a7d4-f7bf-5719-83a5-a5301c0b7f61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6f2a6c54-ca8b-593a-b61e-5ecaccecd8e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32010" :question/problem "Let $$\n\\displaystyle E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of the identity matrix by $-2$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation  ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552496 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f6ba4f-93fb-56ce-b313-ae6f537116c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551677} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa189dd-b632-5f86-b7d8-cf1dd08ab7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551968} {:answer/id #uuid "8f78e22d-2ddc-578a-9218-2dd0858ce54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552015} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ab605b-a2db-549f-a707-66ed6395532a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552056} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe6fa94-e2a0-5a7d-8401-ed49b15524dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552249}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552056} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0e78fb8-ea62-56ea-9a31-70c6851e6dcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b6bf65ad-5479-5fb6-8133-3324438581f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-31997" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix  multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d7d22f-6ff9-5b9a-82a9-bdfe6c4e8376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551679} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb5dd7c-4b48-54a8-b83c-d7defd3de549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551896} {:answer/id #uuid "c76bcf29-916c-5a10-b69c-1134c3821622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552140} {:answer/id #uuid "cae2fb1b-9651-59ca-b1cd-ee01189afa5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552149} {:answer/id #uuid "e4466b78-f73e-5284-a533-d92c2c1c792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552195}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552140} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d002de1-dbdf-5bab-854e-712d27f3c62c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f5b55192-8108-5b5a-9d5a-dfeb97a067b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-75113" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the three given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124ff963-b72f-5e65-b019-142dc4093408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557411} {:answer/id #uuid "495a45f0-bf5a-5f2b-853f-98a9a40f50da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557417} {:answer/id #uuid "be3cc917-c1ca-51f1-b1a3-22d23039ef3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557437} {:answer/id #uuid "cf92e2a8-ab48-5340-bcba-2883848e6c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557439} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ed5e36-0fb0-57ce-baac-38fe4ee2f4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557440}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557437} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba282d53-b116-5cfa-b41a-8b04b5bb86c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2d5b5966-d0b2-51ba-a7a1-c76ebe8e6658" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-5 \\\\ 2x+ky &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-5 \\\\ (k-6)y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c268bc9-b98d-5227-b731-95e04d9c3527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557418} {:answer/id #uuid "ad10948b-c229-52b4-8bd9-550ddae2c192" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557432} {:answer/id #uuid "b131d745-d31e-5a08-8285-4bc65717285c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557433} {:answer/id #uuid "b28ffa47-7c40-5583-883d-0cf4b033e17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557434} {:answer/id #uuid "db4baf4b-c62c-5894-9637-6b82ba9cf1c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557443}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557432} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b3e1241-c1a0-5544-9eae-6f9a638414ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "364e838c-b667-5333-9687-aeee90961e0c" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ -2x+ky &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-3,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27dd0a80-4647-5fb3-bf6e-d022bfd8b7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557412} {:answer/id #uuid "7876e850-f579-5b07-8b9c-174d601fcc57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557425} {:answer/id #uuid "86b4dd02-2b53-599b-a39f-7cdb9621c84d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557426} {:answer/id #uuid "8d82f745-e687-53bf-a943-5f5c160a27c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557429} {:answer/id #uuid "90469b9f-cd36-5eb9-a240-2e5bd047b529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557430}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557412} :answer-field/id #uuid "b669bb3f-c7dc-5f8f-b577-73556f01d6a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4508cab0-6e88-59d6-a9c3-7b9fc61a9c9d" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ 3x+ky &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & k+6 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ (k+6)y &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-6,$ then the second equation is $0=-12,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58b63595-07c3-5725-80e1-8d68eb1d1eac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557420} {:answer/id #uuid "58f14b39-9200-54eb-8f1e-3dda0f24757d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557421} {:answer/id #uuid "60a6d9bd-3eb0-5fbb-8b4c-3b367438cadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #