 :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557410} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce26fa4-9b16-5f35-94ea-df9965919477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557413} {:answer/id #uuid "895f3ba6-7e73-5ee1-88ee-96b78cf55a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557428} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8a51e6-cd68-5ca8-bf4b-3b66c24eddc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557431} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b4341b-24d7-5601-bee0-2b97f2a49be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557442}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557410} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bbf5c12-3409-5553-9dd1-d59b687d99b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4f00ddd-faa4-5195-9569-dbec2d0e2e6c" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-5 \\\\ -2x+ky &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ -2 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ -2 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-5 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-10,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557520 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ccdedd-6990-5c9d-a5e7-669cb20766cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557509} {:answer/id #uuid "1eaab110-0c1d-58e2-a36a-75f81be4b961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3w+1 \\\\ -2w+6 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557511} {:answer/id #uuid "4d74f315-88b3-5c8a-b82e-0c35a568b22d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w-6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557527} {:answer/id #uuid "a82b5c6a-3d85-527b-907c-39a847d234d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557550} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b3d465-f8aa-56d0-aac9-e318dba0f152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557565}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557550} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df2332a-884a-5e30-9bff-9af78c8973ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4149b33c-f03c-5dc8-a587-d4628af75acd" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y-4z+2w &=22 \\\\ 2x+y-z+8w &=16 \\\\ 2x+4w &=12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -4 & 2 & 22 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -4 & 2 & 22 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -2 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2w &=6 \\\\ y+3w &=1 \\\\ z-w &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2w+6 \\\\ y &=-3w+1 \\\\ z &=w-3 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bf4863e-3812-5163-be18-589b2a9762b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w-2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557515} {:answer/id #uuid "4438ccf8-0cf2-5b16-8b50-a324fa882d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557522} {:answer/id #uuid "85ef319c-cf8c-51bd-b6a9-a076f2220193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w-5 \\\\ -2w+2 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557534} {:answer/id #uuid "92a3c94b-a6d0-5d86-a0b4-141b13c2745e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2w+2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557539} {:answer/id #uuid "f2471b96-19e0-554d-9c47-9690ecd4e85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557566}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557566} :answer-field/id #uuid "10d4ff0b-a1ed-57e4-bbde-79ee3d0faaa8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6907b90d-7d23-51a7-95a1-476aee7d4fa3" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y-4z+2w &=-30 \\\\ x+4y+z+7w &=-12 \\\\ -2x-4y+4z-4w &=40.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -4 & 2 & -30 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1 & 7 & -12 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & -4 & 40\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -4 & 2 & -30 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1 & 7 & -12 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & -4 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1 & 7 & -12 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & -4 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 4 & -4 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -2 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -2 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2w &=2 \\\\ y+w &=-5 \\\\ z+w &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2w+2 \\\\ y &=-w-5 \\\\ z &=-w+6 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b7798b-205b-596b-8d7c-8a81288dcdd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}w+4 \\\\ w-6 \\\\ -3w-4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557503} {:answer/id #uuid "534f2668-be2c-5b89-b0db-c3749e56ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}w+6 \\\\ w+4 \\\\ -3w-4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (